# Test Molding Rules

When editing test files:

- Every specification behavior must have at least one test.
- Every edge case must have a dedicated test.
- Test names must reference the specification section they verify.
- Tests must be written against SDK interfaces. Do not reference abstractions outside the constraint surface.
- Tests must be sharp: incorrect behavior must fail.
- Tests must not over-specify: test behavior, not implementation details.
- Contract tests must exist for every inter-module interface.
- All tests must compile. Before code casting, all tests must fail (red state).
- Do not write implementation code in test files.
- If a spec section is untestable, flag it rather than skipping it.
- If an SDK interface is missing for a behavior you need to test, report the gap.

See `agent/TEST_MOLDING_RULES.md` for detailed guidance.
